; ============================================================
; MERGE these sections into the generated Config/DefaultEngine.ini.
; Do NOT replace the file — the Third Person template writes a working
; DefaultEngine.ini (default map, renderer settings, project ID) and losing it
; gives you a project that packages but boots to a black screen.
;
; If a section below already exists, add the keys to it rather than adding a
; second section header; the last duplicate section silently wins.
; ============================================================

[SystemSettings]
; ------------------------------------------------------------
; THE ONE SETTING THIS SAMPLE EXISTS FOR, besides the actor.
;
; FEngineLoop::ShouldUseIdleMode() (Runtime/Launch/Private/LaunchEngineLoop.cpp)
; returns true when ALL of these hold:
;     FApp::IsGame() && FPlatformProperties::SupportsWindowedMode()
;     && t.IdleWhenNotForeground != 0 && !FApp::HasFocus()
; The first two are automatic for a packaged Windows build, so this cvar plus
; alt-tab is a GUARANTEED game-thread stall. Default is 0, and most commercial
; titles ship it off — which is exactly why "find a game that idles when
; backgrounded" had been blocking B8's deferred-restore path.
;
; It cuts both ways, and that is the point:
;   * B8   — alt-tab away, wait >500 ms, click Disable on the Fly card. The
;            deferred collision-restore path is now reachable on demand.
;   * Grausam (foreground lock) — with the lock ON, the WM_ACTIVATEAPP rewrite
;            should keep FApp::HasFocus() true, so idle mode NEVER engages and
;            the game keeps ticking while backgrounded. That is a positive,
;            observable test of the lock rather than "it seemed to keep working".
;
; Set to 0 to turn the sample back into an ordinary always-ticking game.
; ------------------------------------------------------------
t.IdleWhenNotForeground=1
